{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_1da20a10437cc0a60885a64ee2488c4af45a021c523de6751280360a6d540ca0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_ec83dd0a54eece1081ead2972169d1fbc533de6779e8c47647228bd35390ac91"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Each coding thread is bound to its own persistent sandbox; a thread is a durable conversation containing multiple invocations, independent threads run in parallel, and read-only PR chat needs no sandbox.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_48a50b6f1cca70c7d6b6878699a9ad939c23417a1d9d36cd4415866b6e9e2d67","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_b99535898a37bd6d6ea84a3c0f3445d013f05a1fdaf8fbf1180228f6c1645c6c","slc_c96b409864f9df3af082c25ba84e98b47a77b0e90f1437147226fec94c0a83c6"],"source_ids":["src_7b3ceefcc93454a881818cfa6136ac1f"],"text":"The core agent is assembled in a single function, get_agent() in agent/server.py, where the sandbox, model, tools, and triggers can be swapped; custom sandbox providers implement SandboxBackendProtocol from deepagents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_52655e66584a87e1bb3ff6752f0d992b2dc84a1c3c2e38ac6d07175215fce278","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_1c4487b19851279f684277409660d1deb3dd4eed046505b4a8b2f2bf0dc31aa2"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Repository development practice: regenerate swagger.json with make swagger after changing backend routes or models, per the customization documentation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_577b614381fab4418b75ea648d9438ea1082f80f4351c694c135902468d1e5d2","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8854e15d8e1ea24c759996871534a366d5810fa3c2a8c82ec592cd0ebd2fe429","slc_8dcbeb44ec4a7eac28781dfa82437415845f69876f6f019d80fd0deb7a259026","slc_ad4832ef534fa7c36f076bd6a55598ac2ecd4b7c924961cee51b35da0dd1bd54"],"source_ids":["src_7b3ceefcc93454a881818cfa6136ac1f","src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"LangSmith is the default sandbox and tracing provider; Modal, Daytona, Runloop, E2B, and local execution are also supported via a pluggable provider interface selected by the SANDBOX_TYPE environment variable.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_57ae1673933e78fc68cc5af1bc9edbb301a4cd3f050663dc4a67bc7346272d02","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_768562dcf14abc6228993f0e650f055774cef93103a84e8b8996add3229d61b7","slc_d4aa9b9cce008b68237dfb0b9295a682ac5add51143271677cde6b863e7dddf6"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"The system ships five LangGraph graph entrypoints: Agent (implement/validate/deliver changes), Reviewer (read-only PR reviews), Analyzer (learns review style), Chat (PR Q&A), and Scheduler (recurring tasks and CI monitoring).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_676c40853ff37e9148beb3dd2417582aaf7277322c59750fe31050ca74c2b4ca","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0a993a77876b52414cead6d0a8b802cf3c5bed98aab5f4094aee3678d7e2c0df","slc_c770c122e29f4eed16ca816cf6d643fde5d3271a7786028e8f1c065415c02b01"],"source_ids":["src_7b3ceefcc93454a881818cfa6136ac1f"],"text":"Model defaults are configurable via LLM_MODEL_ID and LLM_REASONING_EFFORT; an Anthropic-only deployment defaults to anthropic:claude-opus-5, other deployments to openai:gpt-5.6-sol, with default reasoning effort medium.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_7a7096f91a2eb545640a7b611de43e8f07921697dbbd5829272b7e4e5bfd6c94","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c1765cfa73e1c7244b247ddf3442944fde3fbdb1f8c2505a21679ada5d98f80b"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Safety controls include per-thread sandbox isolation, GitHub App installation boundaries with optional per-user OAuth, org/repo allowlists with actor authorization checks, human approval before pushing workflow-file changes, and read-only reviewer/chat agents.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8709082d819b7fca2d3a86159e6e92c996cfaae5d7142acf31a44a9b5a345815","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_edfb6ff285997ce90f0662d1662fa45c3776053eb1447ff53622087fe4f629a5","slc_f8cd5b34b49a77ad09e9352e08851f4cacdd60243897a2f733819152886062e0"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Open SWE is described as an open-source software factory built on Deep Agents by LangChain, licensed under the MIT License.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8de56af2cfa5a93a1bf4cb0e3cbfcc3c1da84b2dcf97ace0bd6bcd0b2722226d","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_8a0bec6353af8bbf8f7af5008d22642d51bbac19805333420b285a90dbdddfa0","slc_9a926312596ba378133d91f37d0ada0fec618ba2d3a7d6fa23f6deefb50b6748"],"source_ids":["src_7b3ceefcc93454a881818cfa6136ac1f"],"text":"Admins can connect remote MCP servers whose enabled tools become available to all coding-agent users; personal MCP connections load only in private threads owned by the triggering user, and plan mode blocks workspace MCP tools.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9ba0395e23c00fa7a63ba7d2bf9acc190414b8ddeb54af265c21612edb07e4f5","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_c8e00e9d34261d0fccabba18440adb0902c80e13b1cbc709d67e3c3439f8e974","slc_dba1e44d164d0b59104ce5492d5e5668962557e329f7536cd85dd8545abfcbbd"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Repository development practice: local development uses uv venv/uv sync, make build-dashboard, and make dev serving API and dashboard at localhost:2024, with make dev-ui for hot-reloading UI work and an ngrok tunnel exposing only /webhooks/* for webhooks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_aea4b775dd5aeb3ee6a208331d9419381c0290443220776fa6f1a20f1deb481a","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_08b979d9845c55b4b539e39a6a06831140ed76b64f8efabbdf878ef582b5ba15","slc_1c4487b19851279f684277409660d1deb3dd4eed046505b4a8b2f2bf0dc31aa2"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"The custom FastAPI backend (agent.webapp:app) has a generated OpenAPI 3.1 contract in swagger.json, served live at /openapi.json and browsable at /docs; LangGraph runtime endpoints like /runs and /threads are not included in it.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_d9fe1c643132a386b8e356e05b3d4fb227d30657f84769ceefdaae34fb26822e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_598c393e0ed593c2d5e30a1a8df0181296efc316cd452dc67f10a2429df678f0","slc_fd5d016e85c8fae4a6e248f361012cad2463d03c9f44f08fa15694c49a715166"],"source_ids":["src_7b3ceefcc93454a881818cfa6136ac1f","src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"The project is under active development and its APIs, setup, and product surfaces may continue to evolve; the local sandbox provider runs commands directly on the host with no isolation and is intended only for development.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dc22235b02dde51c1de34e7f47ce0c208d31078f8388be408f38db87866d5823","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_04290ed2013e17d500db282938dec7d91f819420a63efcd1db3cd0cced7f07b1"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Cloud work runs in isolated Linux sandboxes that persist with their thread; an unreachable coding sandbox is not silently replaced—the system fails safely rather than risk discarding uncommitted work.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_dca51135bd999b3d67cc382e6545de869ef2db8571144e680b7fe7e3f2c2efa9","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0ac545d0e97e1127a5303933fd553131ada8b9018dcb9d2164c9f99a807c1cb0"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Deep Agents supplies planning, file operations, shell access, skills, state, and subagent primitives; Open SWE adds software-engineering tools, prompts, middleware, integrations, authorization, and product surfaces on top.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_e4a9dc1309f1e3977c989582be20d3107b77829e8af3f0b121ae62b1d9790866","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_768562dcf14abc6228993f0e650f055774cef93103a84e8b8996add3229d61b7"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"LangGraph provides durable execution and thread state, with each Open SWE invocation executing as a LangGraph run within a thread.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_f26c6b8dede45e8fd1dbd978bc158faf62561c576a36b146af11efd8467db946","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5df0ab40f2bfb573c6287cf704a97eef42a204ddaa9230c538f672fbac3e052d","slc_de6db1abfdcdf688234f8469b54375d99832cee5340bec3716ef188c06d0411c","slc_eb21e6833dcb07b9e77658d537ac5dc3986fa3fdd5134f8391f7d54f06ad7c42"],"source_ids":["src_7b3ceefcc93454a881818cfa6136ac1f"],"text":"For LangSmith sandboxes, GitHub proxy rules give github.com Basic auth for git-over-HTTPS and api.github.com Bearer auth for gh/REST; the proxy token is minted at runtime from GitHub App installation credentials rather than stored as env vars.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","created_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_feecdf62a6a0e6a2eca193e583e655be12eed01fd19d531b35ddff32ec96bb41","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"langchain-ai/open-swe@1aa5d3b068c0 snapshot 96ddadd1932f01c2","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_547cf2d1d00eff5384f9efcf8f8554d9926e9f441accb77248f3f42eb3f88d55","slc_689641eb21759994a480604a3c1b676afef03617febb2be0dd25a4f757df6404","slc_7297aaeedd78688a31983c988f84283b0120ef4252f120d8dc94f920db32e353"],"source_ids":["src_8130f6f96f285e65a37437545da05e83"],"text":"Tasks can be started from a web dashboard, GitHub, Slack, or Linear (or on a schedule), and an experimental desktop client runs the agent against local projects, with packaged releases currently targeting macOS.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:10:57Z","updated_by_operation":"op_a42e44b97d324dae98ba2b79642f4a5d"}
